Most enterprise AI never reaches production. Gartner reports that 72% of CIOs are breaking even or losing money on their AI investments. We started&nbsp; Pragyaa&nbsp; to change that. &nbsp; 

We build the platform that runs a company's back office on AI: Legal OS, Finance OS, compliance agents, and an ROI dashboard that shows exactly what the AI delivered. Under all of it sits one ontology, a shared model of the business that connects contracts, ledgers, &nbsp; entities&nbsp; and obligations. &nbsp; 

This is the kind of result it produces. One of our first agents started at 30% accuracy using a frontier model straight out of the box. We added a knowledge graph and got to 70%. Evals, tuning and a live ERP integration took it to 90%. Today it has audited 600+ certificates on its own and gives a 75-year-old real estate company 20+ hours back every week. We now want to do that for every workflow, in every function, and we need the person who designs the system that makes it repeatable. &nbsp; 

What&nbsp; you'll&nbsp; do&nbsp; 

You'll&nbsp; architect the platform, write the pieces that matter most, and take work from design through to production: &nbsp; 

- Design the core platform: &nbsp; the ontology, connectors, agent runtime, model&nbsp; gateway&nbsp; and evaluation layer shared by Legal, Finance, Compliance and ROI reporting. &nbsp; 
 - Write the critical code yourself: &nbsp; the ontology layer, extraction pipelines, &nbsp; orchestration&nbsp; and gateway. &nbsp; 
 - Review and integrate the team's work&nbsp; so every agent works end to&nbsp; end: &nbsp; typed, permissioned, auditable, with human approval where it matters. &nbsp; 
 - Run evaluation-first engineering: &nbsp; golden datasets from real cases, then continuous improvement on accuracy, &nbsp; cost&nbsp; and latency with every model release. &nbsp; 
 - Spend about 30% of your time with customers&nbsp; (general counsels, CFOs, compliance heads) turning their hardest workflows into architecture. The other 70% goes into our own platform, so each engagement makes the product stronger. &nbsp; 

You might be a fit if&nbsp; 

- You've&nbsp; spent 8+ years building software, including 4+ years building AI systems that real enterprise users depend on. &nbsp; 
 - You've&nbsp; designed a knowledge graph or ontology, and you know when a graph beats vector search and when&nbsp; it's&nbsp; overkill. &nbsp; 
 - You've&nbsp; shipped LLM agents or document-extraction systems, and you know how to get from 30% to 90% accuracy. &nbsp; 
 - You think in cost, &nbsp; latency&nbsp; and accuracy together, and you can cut one without breaking the others. &nbsp; 
 - You're&nbsp; comfortable with cloud platforms, APIs, MCP and messy enterprise systems (ERP, CRM, Microsoft 365, Slack). &nbsp; 
 - You'd&nbsp; rather ship than write slide decks, and you can explain your trade-offs to a CFO. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Why join us&nbsp; 

- You own it: &nbsp; you'll&nbsp; be the architect of the platform, working directly with founders who built AI at Google, AWS, &nbsp; Azure&nbsp; and Meta. &nbsp; 
 - It's&nbsp; live: &nbsp; our agents already run legal, &nbsp; finance&nbsp; and compliance work for enterprise customers, from a crypto exchange to a 53-year-old retailer. &nbsp; You'll&nbsp; see your work used in production within weeks, not years. &nbsp; 
 - Results you can measure: &nbsp; every agent you ship reports hours saved and dollar ROI against the customer's own baseline. &nbsp; 
 - Frontier tools: &nbsp; we're&nbsp; a member of the Claude Partner Network and use AI agents across our own engineering, from spec to code to release. &nbsp; 
 - Momentum: &nbsp; we're&nbsp; three years in, with $3M+ ARR and 50+ people across the USA, Canada, the EU and APAC, and&nbsp; we're&nbsp; growing fast. &nbsp;

