Job Brief&nbsp; 

We are looking for an accomplished Technical Program Head with 14-20 years of experience in engineering leadership, technical program management, and large-scale product/program delivery. The candidate should combine strong hands-on technical understanding with exceptional delivery and program management capabilities, with expertise across Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Computer Vision, Physical AI, Robotics, AI infrastructure, and cloud-native platforms. The role will be responsible for driving complex multidisciplinary engineering programs from architecture and planning through development, integration, validation, deployment, and production scale-up. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

• Own end-to-end delivery of multiple strategic AI, robotics, computer vision, and autonomous-system programs. &nbsp; 

• Lead program planning, technical execution, architecture reviews, milestones, dependencies, budgets, risks, and delivery commitments. &nbsp; 

• Translate business and customer requirements into technical roadmaps, program plans, and measurable engineering outcomes. &nbsp; 

• Establish technical governance, architecture standards, engineering best practices, and program delivery frameworks. &nbsp; 

• Drive cross-functional execution across AI/ML, computer vision, robotics, embedded systems, cloud/platform, simulation, QA, DevOps/MLOps, and hardware teams. &nbsp; 

• Lead customer/Tier-1 technical discussions, solution reviews, escalations, and delivery governance. &nbsp; 

• Manage globally distributed engineering teams and engineering leaders. • Drive design and architecture decisions for scalable, reliable, real-time, and safety-critical systems. &nbsp; 

• Establish program KPIs covering schedule, quality, cost, technical maturity, risks, engineering productivity, and customer satisfaction. &nbsp; 

• Drive release planning, integration, validation, deployment, hypercare, and production stabilization. &nbsp; 

• Identify technical and program risks early and establish effective mitigation and recovery plans. &nbsp; 

• Mentor engineering managers, architects, technical leads, and program managers. &nbsp; 

• Drive innovation, technology roadmaps, reusable platforms, IP creation, and engineering excellence. &nbsp; 

Required Skills&nbsp; 

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning&nbsp; 

• Strong expertise in AI/ML, Deep Learning, Foundation Models, Transformers, CNNs, multimodal learning, reinforcement learning, and multi-agent systems. &nbsp; 

• Experience with large-scale model training, optimization, evaluation, and production-grade AI/ML. &nbsp; 

• Strong understanding of Generative AI, representation learning, self-supervised learning, and scalable AI architectures. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Computer Vision & Perception&nbsp; 

• Strong expertise in object detection, classification, segmentation, tracking, depth estimation, and real time image/video analytics. &nbsp; 

• Experience with YOLO, Vision Transformers, Faster R-CNN, SSD, SLAM, multi-view vision, 3D perception, and sensor fusion. &nbsp; 

• Experience building and deploying robust perception systems for industrial, robotic, or autonomous applications. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Robotics & Autonomous Systems&nbsp; 

• Strong experience in autonomous robotic platforms, wheeled/quadrupedal robots, and by wire/autonomous vehicle architectures. &nbsp; 

• Expertise in state estimation, localization, motion planning, low-level control, and hardware-software integration. &nbsp; 

• Working knowledge of ROS/ROS2, Autoware, and real-time robotic/autonomous systems. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Program & Delivery Management&nbsp; 

