Role Summary&nbsp; 

We are seeking an experienced Development Manager to lead a high-performing engineering team responsible for designing, developing, and delivering scalable, high-availability enterprise applications. This role combines strong technical leadership with people management, ensuring engineering excellence, timely delivery, and continuous improvement across the software development lifecycle. &nbsp; 

The ideal candidate is a hands-on technical leader with deep expertise in Java-based backend systems, distributed architectures, and Agile software development, while fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and quality. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

- Lead, mentor, and grow a team of software engineers, fostering a high-performance engineering culture. &nbsp; 

- Drive end-to-end delivery of software projects, ensuring quality, scalability, and timely execution. &nbsp; 

- Provide technical leadership in designing and developing distributed, event-driven, and microservices-based applications. &nbsp; 

- Collaborate with Product Management, Architecture, QA, DevOps, and SRE teams to define technical solutions and delivery plans. &nbsp; 

- Review system architecture, application design, and code to ensure adherence to engineering best practices. &nbsp; 

- Champion engineering excellence through code reviews, automated testing, CI/CD, performance optimization, and secure coding practices. &nbsp; 

- Drive Agile delivery by managing sprint planning, execution, estimations, and release commitments. &nbsp; 

- Identify and mitigate technical risks, remove delivery impediments, and ensure predictable project execution. &nbsp; 

- Support production stability by driving root cause analysis, performance tuning, and continuous operational improvements. &nbsp; 

- Recruit, coach, and develop engineering talent while promoting continuous learning and career growth. &nbsp; 

Required Qualifications&nbsp; 

- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. &nbsp; 

- 13+ years of software development experience, with at least 3+ years in an Engineering or Development Manager role. &nbsp; 

- Strong experience building scalable backend applications using Java and Spring Boot. &nbsp; 

- Hands-on experience with Kafka, multithreading/concurrency, and distributed systems. &nbsp; 

- Strong database expertise with Oracle PL/SQL and relational database design. &nbsp; 

- Experience with containerization and orchestration using Docker and Kubernetes. &nbsp; 

- Strong understanding of microservices architecture, REST APIs, CI/CD pipelines, and Agile development methodologies. &nbsp; 

- Proven experience leading engineering teams and delivering complex enterprise software projects. &nbsp; 

Preferred Skills&nbsp; 

- Experience with cloud platforms (Azure, AWS, or GCP). &nbsp; 

- Familiarity with observability and monitoring tools. &nbsp; 

- Experience in performance tuning, scalability, and high-availability systems. &nbsp; 

- Knowledge of DevSecOps practices and secure software development. &nbsp; 

- Experience working in highly regulated or mission-critical enterprise environments. &nbsp; 

Technical Stack&nbsp; 

- Languages: Java, PL/SQL&nbsp; 

- Frameworks: Spring Boot&nbsp; 

- Messaging: Kafka&nbsp; 

- Concepts: Multithreading, Distributed Systems, Microservices&nbsp; 

- Containers & Orchestration: Docker, Kubernetes&nbsp; 

- Methodologies: Agile, Scrum&nbsp; 

